  "notes": [
    "Logical service names are native.open/native.describe/... per the shared capability contracts. Catalogue names below use the catalogue :: spelling (native::open). The integrator picks final naming.",
    "Every entry keeps the compiler Operation shape (name/identity/kind/receiver/parameters/inputs/staticInputs/result/callbacks/emits/callbackErrors/lowering/assertion/refs) plus a nativeTest block carrying the K01 timing/assimilation/reply/ownership contract. The nativeTest block is advisory metadata for the merge, not a catalogue field.",
    "assertion is supplied: these are supplied external N-service boundaries composed by ordinary Can, not real in-worker computation.",
    "No entry takes an arbitrary module path, export name, eval/source string, or expected-value/oracle argument. Closed enums (native::registered_runtime, native::registered_api, native::registered_operation, native::make_kind, native::observe_kind, native::fault_mode) stay closed; the full enum members are fixed by K02/K03, not here.",
    "Async surface: only native::invoke dispatches a pending action and only native::settle polls it. RPC wrapping adds no thenable read, call, or await; settlement crosses as an inert handle envelope.",
    "Limits: every session carries native::limits with all seven K01 bounds (maxSessions, maxHandlesPerSession, maxPendingActions, maxObserveEntries, maxObserveBytes, maxGatesPerSession, maxFaultsPerSession), each a required positive finite integer. Omitted, zero, negative, fractional, or unlimited bounds reject."
  ],
